word letter S decodes to U. Whether that was intended is unknown."}, {"kind": "omitted_character", "text": "ID BY ROWS", "intended": "WEST X LAYER TWO", "note": "The carved 372-character ciphertext decrypts to an ending of WEST ID BY ROWS. On 19 April 2006 Sanborn disclosed that he omitted an S from the ciphertext (an X in the plaintext) and confirmed the intended reading is 'WEST X LAYER TWO' -- one character longer than the carved ciphertext can support. Ground truth here is what the given ciphertext actually yields, so that a correct decryption is not penalised."}], "scoring_metric": "cer", "scoring_reference": "plaintext_letters_only", "scoring_threshold": 0.0, "source_urls": ["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kryptos", "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/api.php?action=parse&page=Kryptos&prop=wikitext"], "retrieved": "2026-07-30", "sha256_ciphertext": "385bb27d230b5e903ba04b1256cd1a66f10c5dcc0f4f300b6b89f5879eaa714f"}
